course: dictionary
lesson: 13383
title: Where your head rests
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A headrest is the padded part at the top of a seat. It supports the back of your head. You will find one in a car, a plane, a bus or a chair.
explain: Read the words around it to work out its meaning. «Dad told me to adjust the headrest before we drove off.» Adjust means change a little, so a headrest must be something you can move to fit your head.
explain: «In a crash, a good headrest helps to protect your neck.» The clue is protect. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Headrest fits, and the sentence makes sense.
fact: A headrest is the padded part at the top of a seat.
fact: A headrest supports the back of your head.
fact: «Adjust» means change something a little so it fits better.
fact: Car headrests should be set at the right height to help protect your neck in a crash.
fact: Some headrests on planes and buses have screens on the back.
exercise: «Please adjust the headrest so it fits your head.» What does adjust mean? | *Change it a little so it fits better | Sit on it | Wash it in hot water | Remove it and throw it away
exercise: «Mia leaned her head back on the padded headrest of the car seat.» Find and copy the word that means the part that supports your head. | padded | car | *headrest | seat
exercise: «Some headrests on planes have screens on the back.» What is a headrest? | A type of seatbelt | A window blind | A small table for food | *The padded part at the top of a seat that supports your head
test: «A good car headrest protects your neck if the car stops suddenly.» What is the main job of a car headrest? | To hold your bag | To make the seat colder | *To protect your neck in a crash
test: «Dad set the headrest to the right height before we drove off.» What height should a headrest be? | Upside down | *The right height for your head | As high as possible | Lower than the seat
exam: Jayden says, «I can sit on the headrest to get a better view.» Is this a safe use of a headrest? | Only on planes | Yes, if the car is parked | *No, a headrest is for supporting your head, not for sitting on | Yes, that is what it is for
